WEBVTT

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.260
Koizumi-san!

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.510
Misa, Jun, and I are going 
over to Wacky D's now.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.570
Want to join us?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.320
No, thank you.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.690
Rejected again!

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.650
You don't give up, do you?

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.090
What's so great about her, anyway?

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.500
You're really asking that?

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.090
We're talking about 
Koizumi-san here! <i>Koizumi-san</i>!

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.310
She just gets to you.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.970
You can't help but want to get close her!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.300
I can't relate.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.740
All she seems to care about is ramen, 24/7.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.600
Now that you mention it, I've only 
ever talked to her about ramen, too.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.230
And still...

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.750
<i>Why</i>?! Why you two?!

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.470
Why what?

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:53.430
I've tried so many times to 
invite her, only to be rejected!

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.950
So why do you two get to be the ones to 
eat ramen with her like best buddies?

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.040
W-Well, that was just...

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.840
...how things played out.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.950
No fair! No fair! No fair! No fair!

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.490
No fair!

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:10.340
Well, maybe inviting her to 
Wacky D's wasn't the best idea.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.480
That's right.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.470
I mean, does she even eat
anything other than ramen?

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.970
Y-You're right!

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.450
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:36.990
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.910
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.190
<b>Saimin</b>

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.190
Koizumi-san!

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.780
Hey, have you ever been to Wacky D's?

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.450
It might not be your kind of place,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.770
but it's nice every now and then.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.920
You know, while you hang out and talk.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.770
I go there sometimes.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.460
What?! You're kidding!

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.710
This was two months ago.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.360
Excuse me.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.600
I'd like one saimin, please.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.350
Mm-hm. Would you like chopsticks or forks?

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:33.900
Chopsticks.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.610
Okay. Anything else?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.730
No.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.480
Give us a second, please.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.150
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.410
Not at all.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.200
Wait a second!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.850
Wacky D's doesn't sell ramen!

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.480
They do. But only in Hawaii.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.300
They sell a noodle soup called "saimin."

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.240
For real?!

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.560
There are a lot of Japanese 
ramen shops in Hawaii.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.470
I had no trouble finding 
ramen while I was there.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.240
Ezogiku, Tenichi, and Santouka 
aren't the only places.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.700
The flavor at this one place that opened 
recently really hit the spot for me.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.800
It might not be an exaggeration to say that

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.940
after loco moco and macadamia nuts, 
Hawaii is famous for its ramen cuisine.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.320
Wow...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.120
Wait, no! I was trying to find out 
if you've ever eaten a hamburger!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.490
I have.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.750
I had one at Tenichi.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.460
Uh, that's the ramen shop 
we went to that one time.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.160
They didn't have hamburgers.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.250
They do.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:30.200
I don't know why, but it was an item limited 
to the Kireuriwari location in Osaka.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.440
Seriously, why?!

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.020
And that's some name for a restaurant!

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:36.780
The taste was good, the portion size was good,
and the price was good.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.730
Of course, I enjoyed it as
part of a combo with a ramen.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.600
Wow...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.070
Wait, no!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.490
Er... What were we talking about?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:51.740
<b>Kireuriwari</b>

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.370
K... K... Kireuriwari...

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.660
Ki re uri wari

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.080
No... Noeuchindai?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.870
<b>Noeuchindai</b>

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.790
No e uchin dai

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.080
<b>Kizurikamikita</b>

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.900
Kizurikamikita?

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.080
Ki zuri kami kita

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.090
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.010
<b>Flavor Concentration Counter</b>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.920
Koizumi-san!

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.580
Are you free Sunday?

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.840
Want to go somewhere together?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.100
No.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.730
Why not?!

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.270
I want to spend time alone.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.810
Oh, the Kouenji location is out of soup.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.270
Then I'll go to the Shinjuku location.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.630
But you're friends with Misa and Jun!

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.530
I can't accept that I'm the 
only one you're so cold to!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.320
I don't recall becoming anyone's friend.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.580
Can't we just be more friendly?

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.710
We're human beings! We're all one family!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.340
Noodles are my only family.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:50.170
We can go anywhere you like! 
Just take me with you!

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.720
If you're okay with meeting, 
and parting, at the restaurant.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.850
Really?

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.080
Yes! Thank you!

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.060
That's totally fine!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.720
<i>All I need is a foot in the door.</i>

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.860
<i>Once I'm in, we'll be close in no time.</i>

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.540
Koizumi-san!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.030
Why are you wearing your uniform?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.290
I wanted to see you in your regular clothes!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.290
I'm going in.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.120
<b>Open 24/7/365</b>

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.460
Huh?

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.610
Where do we sit? And where are the employees?

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.720
I'll get kaedama today.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.470
I know what kaedama is!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.200
It's when you can get an extra 
portion of just noodles, right?

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.930
I saw it on TV.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.110
I'm getting mine with kaedama, too.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.810
Whee! My first kaedama!

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.060
Seats, hmm...

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.970
Looks like the two ends have openings.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.650
A map of free seats?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:47.480
What is this?

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.420
See you when we're done.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.940
Uh, do we sit in the back?

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.550
<i>A cubicle?</i>

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.450
<i>This is like a study booth or something!</i>

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.710
<b>Packed</b>

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.710
<i>Koizumi-san is so far away!</i>

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.210
<b>Here</b>

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:02.710
<b>Here</b>

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.000
Talk about being forced to sit alone.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:12.170
<b>Please mark all fields
 Flavor Intensity: Light, Medium, Strong
Heaviness: None, Light, Medium, Heavy, Very Heavy
Garlic: None, Little, Medium, More, Double
Onion: None, White, Green
Chashu Pork: Yes, No
Secret Sauce: None, Half, x1, x2, x(_)
Noodle Firmness: Very Firm, Firm, Regular, Soft, Very Soft</b>

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:12.170
"Let us know your preferences"?

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.930
Might as well get the standard, 
since it's my first time.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.670
All right. Done.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.080
I wonder where the wait staff is.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.640
I'm so bored.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.150
Pardon me.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.800
I've reviewed your order and 
it will be coming shortly.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.060
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.530
<i>There was someone back there?!</i>

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.200
<i>I'll get my usual.</i>

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.540
<i>Noodle firmness...</i>

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:50.250
<b>Noodle Firmness: Very Firm, Firm, Regular, Soft, Very Soft</b>

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:45.690
<i>They don't do yugedoushi or konaotoshi here,</i>

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:49.480
<i>so I want to get the firmest one they offer.</i>

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:54.810
<i>But since I just had a bowl at 
the new place by the station,</i>

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.510
<b>Second
bowl
today</b>

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.510
<i>I'll order "soft" now.
It's easier on the stomach.</i>

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:04.020
Aw, man... What was even 
the point of coming here?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.410
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.910
Pardon me.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.020
I-It closed again...

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.580
This tonkotsu looks amazing.

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.260
Time to eat.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.910
<i>These thin noodles are so good!</i>

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:39.090
Now... what about the extra noodles?

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.100
I guess I do this.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.100
<b>Kaedama</b>

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:47.060
<b>Kaedama</b>

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.400
<b>Set plate with ticket here</b>

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.480
<b>Order</b>

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.940
Thank you for waiting. Here's your kaedama.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:56.760
Wow!

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:07.870
<i>It felt pretty sad at first, 
sitting here all alone,</i>

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:13.510
<i>but ramen is great even 
when you eat it by yourself!</i>

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.970
<b>Tennen Tonkotsu Ramen 		Ichiran</b>

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:18.970
That was great.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.040
Goodbye, then.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.100
Yeah. See you at school!

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:33.140
<i>We didn't talk at all.</i>

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.300
<i>The ramen was delicious, though.</i>

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.660
By the way, those partitions can be moved.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.700
Koizumi-san, next time we totally 
need to sit next to each other!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.450
No, thank you.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.960
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.460
<b>Your Basket</b>

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:57.460
<b>Instant Noodles</b>

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:02.200
My brother won't be home today.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.470
Let's do something simple...

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.470
<b>Ramen • Noodles</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:07.470
I'm thinking ramen.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:12.210
I wonder if Koizumi-san has a 
favorite brand of instant ramen.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.690
She's always eating it at school.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:23.200
Someday, I want to make ramen for 
Koizumi-san and have her eat it.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:26.460
I wonder if she likes to add her own touches.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.700
Oh, I bet this would be good with it.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.940
<b>It's delicious</b>

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.530
It's delicious.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.940
<b>Oh, my...</b>

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:32.560
Oh, my...

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:38.000
One day, I'll use my skills from home ec 
club and being on kitchen duty

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.470
at home to make something for Koizumi-san...

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:45.970
Thinking about Koizumi-san 
made me get all this.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.140
Oh, well...

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.230
It'll get eaten.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.480
<b>Your Basket</b>

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:53.040
Thank you.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:03.140
I wonder what kind of ramen 
Koizumi-san is eating right now...

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.210
Koizumi-san?!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.040
Should we call an ambulance?

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.590
Koizumi-san, what's wrong?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.300
I can't believe I did this.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.130
This place is always closed today.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.300
<b>Chinese Cuisine  Ikomaken</b>

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.300
<b>Closed 
Today</b>

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.300
You collapsed because you're starving?!

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:27.110
I don't really know what's going on,
but I'll carry you to my house.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.360
It's close!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.600
<i>Actually...</i>

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.800
<i>I think this is the first time 
I've ever touched her.</i>

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.990
Now isn't the time for that!

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.650
Hang in there, Koizumi-san! It's not far!

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.270
Such passion.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.750
<b>Ohsawa</b>

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.200
Where am I?

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.120
Oh, you're awake.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.450
I was thinking I should 
probably wake you soon.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:12.540
By the way, it's evening already.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.360
Huh?

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:16.760
You collapsed by that ramen place nearby.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:17.520
Do you remember?

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.900
I forgot which day they're closed.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:24.720
I hadn't eaten anything since morning,
so all my strength left me.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:33.120
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.040
Hold on!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.620
Why don't you eat before you go?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.080
I was just making dinner.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:41.240
You might not think it,
but I'm actually good at cooking.

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:44.340
Both my parents work,
so I've been doing it since I was a kid.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.700
I'm even in the home ec club.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.720
Not that I ever attend, but...

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:01.360
What's this?

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.230
My famous mock Italian ramen.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:14.240
<b>Salt</b>

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.720
You can use any soup for the base.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.380
You boil the instant noodles in tomato juice,

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:14.240
then you stir-fry garlic, 
leftover vegetables, and meat.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.990
For meat, you can even use bacon or wieners.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:20.880
Before serving, you season with fresh ground 
pepper and a sprinkle of cheese, and it's done.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:25.220
If you put that much work into it,
it can't really be called "instant" anymore.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:27.120
But it's super easy!

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.880
It's totally instant!

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:34.390
I usually settle for something much simpler.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.770
<b>"Oroshi Soba Ramen"</b>

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.640
Take soy sauce ramen, 
dump on tempura flakes,

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.770
grated daikon radish,
and shaved bonito flakes.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:44.900
<b>"Pizza Chips Ramen"</b>

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.600
Take miso ramen, dump on 
crumbled potato chips

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:44.900
and melted cheese, and season 
to taste with Tabasco sauce.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:48.030
<b>Tuna Rice Ball Ramen</b>

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.030
Take salt ramen, and dump on 
canned tuna and dried nori.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:56.040
<b>Oroshi Soba Ramen</b>

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:56.040
<b>Pizza Chips Ramen</b>

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:56.040
<b>Tuna Rice Ball Ramen</b>

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.760
Lately, there are many types 
of ramen that are loved for

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.660
their non-instant feel and 
compatibility with simple ingredients.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.750
It's very helpful.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.040
<i>She only dumps stuff on!</i>

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.240
But that aside, is it all right if I eat now?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.210
Please go ahead!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.450
Time to eat.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.930
<b>Ba-dump</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.930
<b>Ba-dump</b>

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.070
<b>Slurp
Slurp
Slurp</b>

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.750
<b>Glug
Glug
Glug</b>

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.760
Exquisite.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.590
<b>Finished.</b>

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.590
May I have some more?

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.850
I'm so glad!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.480
You always eat at ramen shops,

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.350
so I was worried you might say,
"This isn't ramen," or something.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:08.530
The beauty of restaurant ramen and
homemade ramen are completely different.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:11.860
It's meaningless to argue over which is better.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.040
You're absolutely right...

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:17.120
On that note, I'll make you some more.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.370
What kind would you like?

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.750
I could do Chinese, Taiwanese, or Thai flavors.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.660
If you'd like to switch it up,

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:28.160
mixing crushed noodles with rice 
to make chicken fried rice

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:30.760
or a soy milk risotto can be quite good, too.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:34.380
Those things don't have much left to 
do with ramen, but they do sound good.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.350
Anyway, I'll try all of those.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.510
Okay, got it!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.820
Just leave it to me.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.700
<i>This is so strange.</i>

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:06.520
<i>I'm here at home, and everything is like 
it always is, except Koizumi-san is here.</i>

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:10.860
<i>It's almost like we're...</i>

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:20.600
I started with a soy sauce base, added egg
and veggies, then thickened it with starch.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.850
Hot and sour noodles!

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.480
If you like, go ahead and add vinegar!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.020
Sweet and sour...

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.910
Next, a miso base, with an added can 
of mackerel and some curry roux!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.180
It's mackerel miso curry ramen!

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.120
The uncanny alliance of miso and curry!

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.130
And there's still more!

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:57.630
Start with a tonkotsu base, add bacon, milk, 
and a poached egg for carbonara-style ramen!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.640
The still-runny yolk mingles 
with the tonkotsu!

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.480
And on top of that!

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.220
To finish, a dish prepared cold!

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:12.980
Ochazuke-flavored ramen with 
ground chicken and pickled plum!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.490
Strong green tea ties the dish together.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.930
So how was it?

00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:00.320
Are you full now?

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.590
I am very satisfied.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.690
That's good to hear.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:10.430
I will definitely make this up to you.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:13.110
Oh, you don't have to...

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:20.640
Good morning.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:21.340
Good morning.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.720
Good morning!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:25.280
Why are you grinning at this hour?

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:28.460
You look happy, but it's also... scary.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:35.610
Oh, I just had a wonderful day yesterday.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.160
What's all this?

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:49.500
Ramen coupons?

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:52.300
Where'd they come from?

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:53.600
No idea...

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.440
Oh, Koizumi-sa—

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.930
To thank you for yesterday.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:58.380
She ran away!

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.480
Koizumi-san!

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.840
Does this mean you want to go eat with me?

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:14.980
It does not.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.360
Please enjoy them by yourself.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.240
Oh, come on!

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.510
You're coming with me, aren't you?

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.920
No, thank you.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.040
I'm so excited!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.880
Who knew there were this many coupons?

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:31.900
Lately, these things are mainly 
put up on social networks,

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:34.480
but there are still a lot of 
paper coupons out there.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Western Restaurant</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Red or White</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Convenience Store</b>

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:15.300
So, Koizumi-san, you can 
actually speak English?

00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:17.390
Enough to have a conversation.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:19.180
How did you learn it?

00:22:19.180 --> 00:22:21.980
Do you go to cram school, or one 
of those language schools by

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.950
the station, or do you have someone 
around you to practice with?

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:25.990
It's a secret.

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:28.080
Another secret, huh?

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:36.000
<b>Thank you for the food!</b>
